    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "4e2a103ff8c9b480b877adf87bc2ff12",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Notice order 3 disappeared. Its amount is NULL, <code>10 &lt; NULL</code> is NULL\n(\"unknown\"), and a filter only keeps rows whose condition is <strong>true</strong>.\nKeep that in mind; it is the source of most surprises below.</span>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-theorem-looks-like\">What a theorem looks like</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Optimizers constantly rewrite plans into faster, <em>supposedly equivalent</em>\nones. A classic rewrite merges two filters:</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>Filter(Filter(r, p), q)</code> \u27f6 <code>Filter(r, p AND q)</code></span>\n</blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Here is how <code>SubstraitLean/Rewrites.lean</code> states and proves it:</span>\n<div class=\"language-lean codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">filter_filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rel</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Catalog</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List.filter_filter</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr.eval</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BinFn.apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isTrue_and3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool.and_comm</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">How to read it:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Piece</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>theorem filter_filter</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">the claim's name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>(r : Rel) (p q : Expr) (cat : Catalog)</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>for every</strong> plan <code>r</code>, every two conditions <code>p</code>, <code>q</code>, and every database <code>cat</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>\u2026 .eval cat = \u2026 .eval cat</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">both plans return exactly the same rows</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>:= by simp [...]</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">the proof: unfold the definitions and simplify. Lean checks every step mechanically</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The \"for every\" is the whole point. A test picks <em>some</em> <code>r</code>, <code>p</code>, <code>q</code> and\nsome data; the theorem covers <strong>all</strong> of them, including tables with\nmillions of rows you will never generate.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The proof relies on one small fact, <code>isTrue_and3</code>: <code>p AND q</code> is true\nexactly when both <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> are true, <em>even with NULLs</em>. That fact only\ninvolves a handful of cases, so we can check every one of them right here,\nwhich is exactly what Lean's proof does (it splits into cases and checks\neach):</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "518d90aa4d6e9a28b43c4d81fffdcd01",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>p</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>q</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>p AND q</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>keep? (merged)</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>keep? (two filters)</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>same</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>true</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>false</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>\u2713</td></tr></tbody></table>"
